    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If in the land which the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God gives you to possess, any one is found slain, lying in the open country, and it is not known who killed him, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "then your elders and your judges shall come forth, and they shall measure the distance to the cities which are around him that is slain; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and the elders of the city which is nearest to the slain man shall take a heifer which has never been worked and which has not pulled in the yoke. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the elders of that city shall bring the heifer down to a valley with running water, which is neither plowed nor sown, and shall break the heifer's neck there in the valley. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the priests the sons of Levi shall come forward, for the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God has chosen them to minister to him and to bless in the name of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", and by their word every dispute and every assault shall be settled. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And all the elders of that city nearest to the slain man shall wash their hands over the heifer whose neck was broken in the valley; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and they shall testify, ‘Our hands did not shed this blood, neither did our eyes see it shed. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Forgive, O ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", thy people Israel, whom thou hast redeemed, and set not the guilt of innocent blood in the midst of thy people Israel; but let the guilt of blood be forgiven them.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So you shall purge the guilt of innocent blood from your midst, when you do what is right in the sight of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“When you go forth to war against your enemies, and the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God gives them into your hands, and you take them captive, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and see among the captives a beautiful woman, and you have desire for her and would take her for yourself as wife, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "then you shall bring her home to your house, and she shall shave her head and pare her nails. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And she shall put off her captive's garb, and shall remain in your house and bewail her father and her mother a full month; after that you may go in to her, and be her husband, and she shall be your wife. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then, if you have no delight in her, you shall let her go where she will; but you shall not sell her for money, you shall not treat her as a slave, since you have humiliated her.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“If a man has two wives, the one loved and the other disliked, and they have borne him children, both the loved and the disliked, and if the first-born son is hers that is disliked, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "then on the day when he assigns his possessions as an inheritance to his sons, he may not treat the son of the loved as the first-born in preference to the son of the disliked, who is the first-born, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "DEU 21:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but he shall acknowledge the first-born, the son of the disliked, by giving him a double portion of all that he has, for he is the first issue of his strength; the right of the first-born is his.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "DEU.21.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "DEU.21.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
